# lbtest's second set-up (command line "2"): B has 3 items and LBS_DISABLENOSCROLL (seg43:0000 only
# enables / disables the bars it was created with: both stay, all arrows disabled), C is an empty owner-draw
# list. USER's behaviour checked (values from the seg35 decode, screenshots checked by eye):
# - clicking the empty C gives it the focus: its owner gets WM_DRAWITEM itemID -1, ODA_FOCUS, state
#   ODS_FOCUS | ODS_SELECTED (seg35:085C asks IsSelected for a missing item: -1, "selected"); no
#   WM_LBTRACKPOINT (no item);
# - a double click on A's item 2: LBN_SELCHANGE for the first click, only LBN_DBLCLK for the second,
#   WM_LBTRACKPOINT for the first click only;
# - Ctrl+\ keeps only the caret item; Shift+F8 add mode: Down, Down, Space adds item 4 without
#   dropping 2 (each key notifies LBN_SELCHANGE).
# regress: sh apps/lbtest/tests/lbtest.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" 2
# ini: LBTEST.INI B vbar=1
# ini: LBTEST.INI B hbar=1
# ini: LBTEST.INI C count=0
# ini: LBTEST.INI C vbar=0
# ini: LBTEST.INI A sel=2,4
# ini: LBTEST.INI A caret=4
# ini: LBTEST.INI A anchor=4
# ini: LBTEST.INI events selchangeA=5
# ini: LBTEST.INI events dblclkA=1
# ini: LBTEST.INI events setfocusC=1
# ini: LBTEST.INI events track=1,101,2,10,40
# ini: LBTEST.INI events drawlog=-1:4:11;-1:4:1;
sleep 300
click 60 240
sleep 200
shot shots/01-empty-focus.png
dblclick 34 83
key ctrl+backslash
key shift+f8
key down
key down
key space
key shift+f8
sleep 200
shot shots/02-addmode.png
quit
